NUM-51: return 0, not NaN, for a fractional power of a negative number

The expression evaluators (math/MathExpr.cpp for [GWF] and control rules,
quality/Treatment.cpp for [TREATMENT]) call std::pow directly, so (-4)^0.5
is NaN and the NaN becomes the result, e.g. a node concentration. Use the
legacy rule, as corrected for 5.3.0 by this issue: pow() for a positive base
and for a negative base with a whole-number exponent, 0 otherwise (fractional
power of a negative number, zero base).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-51_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/math/MathExpr.cpp b/src/engine/math/MathExpr.cpp
index 4eb512e..da8435d 100644
--- a/src/engine/math/MathExpr.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/math/MathExpr.cpp
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@ double evaluate(const Expression& expr,
                     case TokenType::SUB: stk.push(a-b); break;
                     case TokenType::MUL: stk.push(a*b); break;
                     case TokenType::DIV: stk.push(b!=0?a/b:0); break;
-                    case TokenType::POW: stk.push(std::pow(a,b)); break;
+                    case TokenType::POW: stk.push((a > 0.0 || (a < 0.0 && b == std::floor(b))) ? std::pow(a,b) : 0.0); break;
                     default: break;
                 }
                 break;
@@ -397,7 +397,8 @@ double evaluate_fast(const Expression& expr, const double* vars) noexcept {
             }
             case TokenType::POW: {
                 double b=stk[--sp];
-                stk[sp-1] = std::pow(stk[sp-1], b); break;
+                double a=stk[sp-1];
+                stk[sp-1] = (a > 0.0 || (a < 0.0 && b == std::floor(b))) ? std::pow(a, b) : 0.0; break;
             }
             case TokenType::FUNC_ABS:  stk[sp-1] = std::fabs(stk[sp-1]); break;
             case TokenType::FUNC_SQRT:
